## API

API base URL:

- `https://api.practicesoftwaretesting.com`

Environment variables:

- `API_BASE_URL` is used only by the Playwright `api` project and API tests;
- `UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL` is used by `src/test/fixtures/api-preconditions.fixture.ts` for UI API precondition setup;
- `UI_API_BASE_URL` is an optional fallback for UI API precondition setup when `UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL` is not provided;
- UI precondition API base must point to the same backend used by UI runtime API calls.

UI precondition fixture ownership and usage:

- `registrationApiPreconditionSetup` is owned by `src/test/fixtures/api-preconditions.fixture.ts`;
- fixture exposure follows `api-preconditions.fixture.ts` -> `pages.fixture.ts` -> `test.ts`;
- UI specs must use the fixture for API setup and keep UI action under test explicit in spec steps;
- setup through `registrationApiPreconditionSetup` verifies only required precondition creation success and returns created user credentials;
- UI specs must not read environment variables directly;
- UI specs must not derive API host from UI host.

API documentation / contract source:

- `https://api.practicesoftwaretesting.com/api/documentation`

API docs type:

- Swagger UI / OpenAPI 3.0

API specs:

- `tests/api/**/*.api.spec.ts`

API Playwright project:

- `api`

API clients:

- `src/test/api/clients/`

API schemas:

- `src/test/api/schemas/`

API types:

- `src/test/api/types/`

Rules:

- API tests must use the API documentation as contract source;
- API tests must not guess payload fields, status codes, or response fields;
- if the API contract is unclear or incomplete, stop and report missing information;
- API tests use request/response model;
- API tests must not use Page Objects;
- API tests must not use Component Objects;
- API tests must not use browser page interactions;
- API clients are thin and optional;
- API clients must not contain assertions;
- API clients must not use Allure;
- API specs may use the shared Allure metadata helper.


## Test Strategy

Rules:

- use the lowest reliable test level;
- do not default to UI tests;
- feature plans must include recommended test level per scenario;
- avoid duplicate coverage across UI, API, visual, and schema tests.

Skill:

- `.cursor/skills/plan-test-coverage/SKILL.md`

