## TMS Integration

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/tms-integration.rules.mdc`

Provider:

- Qase

Stable project code:

- `TOOLSSHOP`

Project MCP (`.cursor/mcp.json`):

- `playwright` — project-level MCP; safe to commit in repo

Qase MCP:

- server name: `qase`
- configured in user/global Cursor MCP settings (not in project `.cursor/mcp.json`)
- requires `QASE_API_TOKEN` in user/global MCP config; never commit real tokens to repo

Default mode:

- read-only

Feature plan mapping location:

- `specs/<feature>.md`

Required TMS sections in feature plans:

- TMS Source
- TMS Mapping

Plan from TMS:

- skill: `.cursor/skills/plan-from-tms/SKILL.md`
- command: `.cursor/commands/plan-from-tms.md`

Align plan with TMS:

- skill: `.cursor/skills/align-plan-with-tms/SKILL.md`
- command: `.cursor/commands/align-plan-with-tms.md`

No-existing-plan workflow:

1. `/plan-from-tms`
2. review generated plan
3. implement selected ready API/UI coverage

Existing-plan workflow:

1. `/plan-feature`
2. `/align-plan-with-tms`
3. review aligned plan
4. implement selected ready API/UI coverage

Principles:

- TMS cases are planning input and traceability source
- do not assume 1 TMS case equals 1 Playwright test
- align TMS intent with feature plans; do not replace plans blindly
- API owns backend contract and data predicates
- UI owns distinct user-facing browser behavior
- undocumented negative/boundary behavior must be blocked/postponed, not guessed

TMS writes:

- require explicit user approval
- no create/update/delete/reorder/run/result publishing by default

Secrets:

- real Qase tokens must not be committed
- real Qase tokens must not be stored in docs, rules, skills, commands, specs, or committed MCP config

Reporter status:

- Qase reporter/result publishing is not configured yet
